   :doc "Dismiss a recovery run that is over and left its cause owed: settle what it named without restoring it, so it is not retried. :run <run-id> [:note \"…\"]"
   :task (apply nido-recovery/dismiss-cmd *command-line-args*)}

  nido:recovery:restore
  {:requires ([tasks.nido-recovery :as nido-recovery])
   :doc "Restore the owed failures of a recovery run's cause: start each session a person was in here, withdraw a start made for a run or a reply, record each outcome on the run. Refuses without a recorded :session-diagnosis. [:run <run-id>, default the calling turn's run]"
   :task (apply nido-recovery/restore-cmd *command-line-args*)}

  nido:recovery:land
  {:requires ([tasks.nido-recovery :as nido-recovery])
   :doc "Land a recovery's nido fix: refuses unless the diagnosis names a nido defect and bb nido:test and bb nido:land:check pass at the worktree's tip on origin's main; then fast-forwards main and records the :merged on the run. [:run <run-id>, default the calling turn's run] [:cwd <dir>]"
   :task (apply nido-recovery/land-cmd *command-line-args*)}

